        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ناشر",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ناشر — nāshir — \"a publisher\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قبل الناشر كتاب أختي. qabila an-nāshir kitāb ukhtī. The publisher accepted my sister’s book."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A publishing house is دار نشر."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ناشر (nāshir) is built on the native Arabic root n-sh-r (Lane), \"to spread out\", the root of the taught nashara. Nāshir is the active participle, \"one who publishes\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
